  "identity_policy": "Preserve accepted lady-slipper/orchid dancer evolution identities, anatomy, individual palettes and stage silhouettes. This proposal contains art only; do not modify profiles, stats, types or moves.",
  "design_notes": "Identity-preserving six-view refinement: golden round leaf-pouch and hood, lilac S-stem dancer with two white shoulder petals and two pouch slippers, then forest-green orchid dancer with three white/pink crown sepals, two leaf arms, three separate pink hip petals and two slipper feet. Exact existing individual palettes retained. SourceBacked avoids dense black leaf interiors; white8 on Slipperina/Cyprielle fronts keeps eye and face separators while all rear portraits use white4. The large white petals have closed dark anchors and broad colored roots; no extra limbs, generic gown or full-body rear. Front native sizes56x56, backs48x48; silhouettes36/44/54 and close46x47maximum.",
